@page "/introduction"

<SeoHead Title="Build application UI with Quark | Quark Suite" Description="Composable Blazor components inspired by shadcn/ui, with typed styling, generated assets, and examples you can adapt to your application." />

<DocumentationPage Title="Build application UI with Quark" Description="Composable Blazor components inspired by shadcn/ui, with typed styling, generated assets, and examples you can adapt to your application.">

<Section Id="start-with-a-real-interface">
    <H2>Start with a real interface</H2>
    <Paragraph>Quark gives you the building blocks for application screens: forms and validation, navigation and layouts, dialogs, data tables, charts, feedback, and AI/chat interfaces. Use the default component styles to get a working screen, then adapt the design without changing how you write Blazor.</Paragraph>
<Paragraph><Anchor Href="installation">Install Quark</Anchor> → <Anchor Href="first-component">build your first component</Anchor> → <Anchor Href="components">explore the catalog</Anchor>.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="composition">
    <H2>Work with the parts of a component</H2>
    <Paragraph>Compose a card from its header, content, and actions. Compose a dialog from its trigger and content. Keep input state and event handlers in C#, and pass ordinary HTML attributes where you need them.</Paragraph>
    <CodeEditor Text="@navigation" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
    <Paragraph>This example uses <Code>AsChild</Code> to give a real navigation link the button's visual treatment. Use a button for an action and an anchor for navigation; composition lets you keep the right element.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="styling">
    <H2>Choose how much styling you want to write</H2>
    <Paragraph>Start with variants such as <Code>ButtonVariant.Outline</Code>. Reach for typed properties when you need spacing, sizing, responsive layout, and semantic colors. Use <Code>Class</Code> and <Code>Style</Code> for precise custom treatment.</Paragraph>
    <CodeEditor Text="@chain" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
    <Paragraph>A modifier configures the next value in the chain. Here, <Code>OnX.Is4</Code> produces horizontal padding and <Code>OnMd.Row</Code> changes the layout at the medium breakpoint. <Anchor Href="properties">Learn the builder model</Anchor>.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="build-assets">
    <H2>Your .NET build prepares the assets</H2>
    <Paragraph>Quark's generators turn source-visible classes, icon names, and theme definitions into assets the browser can use. The Tailwind build provisions Node.js/npm when needed. Icon generators create SVG maps and service registrations. An optional theme generator writes CSS from C#.</Paragraph>
    <Paragraph>You install the relevant packages, enable the CSS build, and run <Code>dotnet build</Code>. The <Anchor Href="generators">generator guide</Anchor> explains the inputs, outputs, and which packages an application actually needs.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="behavior">
    <H2>Interaction behavior comes from Bradix</H2>
    <Paragraph>Quark uses Bradix primitives for interactions such as focus management, overlays, and composite controls. Bradix is already a suite dependency and is registered by <Code>AddQuarkSuiteAsScoped()</Code>. Your application still supplies meaningful labels, keyboard-friendly flows, and appropriate validation messages.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="shadcn">
    <H2>Familiar design, native Blazor usage</H2>
    <Paragraph>shadcn/ui informs Quark's visual language, naming, variants, and composition. Quark is distributed as an MIT-licensed NuGet library and uses Razor and .NET APIs. There is no React app or shadcn CLI setup to maintain.</Paragraph>
    <Paragraph>Use <Anchor Href="themes">theme tokens</Anchor> to make the controls fit your product. The app-owned C# theme and stylesheet order documented here follow patterns used in Leadping; the public <Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.blazor.creditcards/tree/main/test/Soenneker.Blazor.CreditCards.Demo">CreditCards demo</Anchor> is a smaller reference for Quark and icon registration.</Paragraph>
</Section>

